extraction_notes: "Page span: the heading starts partway down printed 84 and the entry ends at the foot of printed 85; the next class starts on printed 86. GROUP: the book''s Coalition Military O.C.C.s section (printed 67), so men-of-arms and men_of_arms true. The +2D6 physical S.D.C. is stored as a pools bonus on top of the core roll. MONEY: 1D6x1000 credits to start as printed; base salary 2,050 credits a month. The text layer reads the dice as a cipher; confirmed 1D6x1000 and 2050 from a render. THE BOOK PRINTS NO LANGUAGE SKILL for this class, only Literacy: American; none is added. RIFLE: the book prints \"CP-40 or C-50\"; this book calls the CP-50 Dragonfire the C-50 elsewhere (printed 78), so the choice is the CP-40 and the CP-50. E-clips: four for the rifle and one for the pistol, stored as five. Light or heavy Dead Boy is offered as this book''s CA-3 light and CA-4 standard (printed 100 says the army typically wears one of those two). The older CA-1 heavy is not offered: printed 104 makes the old style exclusive to the ISS. This book''s own new heavy suit is the CA-6EX exoskeleton, an infantry augmentation suit, and is not offered to a pilot. Fine leather gloves are stored as the plain gloves row. The hovercycle or jeep is a vehicle and lives in restrictions, as the Side Kick RPA does; see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F3. The two special piloting abilities have their own base skills and stay as special abilities; the catalog''s Hovercycles, Skycycles & Rocket Bikes row is a different, general skill."
