## Lore

The 53rd Group is the branch of the Coalition Army that flies combat aircraft,
power armor and robots. Its Aces, the "Fly Boys", are capable power armor
pilots but specialise in aircraft, above all the many kinds of skycycle.

A demanding course builds on RPA school: instrument night-flying, special-ops
fire support, radar avoidance, and long hours in simulators and cockpits. Those
who pass wear the 53rd''s combat patch and fly troop drops, resupply and
extraction, cover and support fire, rescues, surgical strikes, patrols, strafing
runs and frontline power armor assaults.

## GM Notes

Fly Boys are brash, wisecracking and arrogant in quiet times, and dependable
and daring in a firefight.

On assignment: grenades, explosives, mission weapons, optics, cameras and
surveillance gear, rations, and any vehicle, power armor or robot suited to the
mission that the ace can fly. Security clearance runs mid-level to top.
